StatProdFailPortion [SimTalk] - Drain
Returns the portion of the sum of all life times of the MUs during which these stayed on a failed material
flow object of resource type Production, and which the Drain designated by <Path> removed from the
plant.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.StatProdFailPortion → real
Return Value
The return value has the data type real.
Example
var ra: real
ra := Drain.StatProdFailPortion + Drain.StatStoreFailPortion + 
Drain.StatTranspFailPortion
if ra > 0.6 
   print "Considerable delays caused by failed machines."
end
See also
Resource Type of the material flow objects
Tab Type Statistics of the Drain
Statistics report, Cumulated Statistics of the Parts which the Drain Removed From the Plant
StatProdFailPortion [SimTalk] - Drain
Plant Simulation Help 11-1673
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

